%N A361525 Number of ways of dividing an n X 3 rectangle into integer-sided rectangles, up to rotations and reflections.
%H A361525 Pontus von Brömssen, <a href="/A361525/b361525.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..1000</a> (terms 0..200 from Duncan Marc Bentley)
%H A361525 Duncan Marc Bentley, <a href="/A361525/a361525.txt">Python program</a>.
%H A361525 <a href="/index/Rec#order_11">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (21,-137,171,1534,-5778,2056,20304,-30253,-5151,35241,-18207).
%F A361525 a(n) >= A208215(n)/4 for n != 3.
%F A361525 a(n) ~ A208215(n)/4.
%F A361525 a(n) ~ C*r^(n-1), where r = 10.018092436973715... is the largest root of x^3 - 15*x^2 + 55*x - 51 and C = (2*r^2-13*r+16)/(2*(3*r^2-30*r+55)) = 0.778567728154495... . - _Pontus von Brömssen_, Nov 14 2026
%F A361525 a(n) = 21*a(n-1) - 137*a(n-2) + 171*a(n-3) + 1534*a(n-4) - 5778*a(n-5) + 2056*a(n-6) + 20304*a(n-7) - 30253*a(n-8) - 5151*a(n-9) + 35241*a(n-10) - 18207*a(n-11) for n >= 15. - _Pontus von Brömssen_, Nov 16 2026
%t A361525 LinearRecurrence[{21, -137, 171, 1534, -5778, 2056, 20304, -30253, -5151, 35241, -18207}, {1, 3, 17, 54, 892, 8159, 80021, 791821, 7906439, 79069308, 791689234, 7929071619, 79426483207, 795665694992, 7970910913358}, 25] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Nov 16 2026 *)
